{"id": "EUVD-2026-80537", "enisaUuid": "ff6b0eb5-12e5-35a3-8817-c8087f7c8955", "description": "In the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:\n\niio: chemical: sgp30: Handle IAQ thread creation failure\n\nkthread_run() can fail and return an error pointer, but sgp_probe() stores\nit and returns success, so the device is registered without its IAQ thread\nand sgp_remove() later passes the error pointer to kthread_stop(). Return\nthe error from probe instead.", "datePublished": "2026-09-16T10:32:26", "dateUpdated": "2026-10-19T08:55:11", "baseScore": 0.0, "references": ["https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/bffd0655a35402b2df8857699f8248e5a534d214", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/bae0316c087b1ef625844003fe37e803a13819f3", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/3c6b52b258e65a584e3f5122ed7f406bc89a946e", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/3462c13bb0f50dec09235adb7fd04b6f617cf0cc", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/a5aaea17a1834d7254ff597e4d5e1bc60dfc4800", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/2d386efb4c37a50739db19c7c8e49564fd53a570", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/44d52c8b1c6da7ac1b0dffeeff6de68370746775", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/1135d6875d2dbda3f6ec718f3421a6ce4378bd63"], "aliases": ["CVE-2026-89937", "GHSA-gxqw-4h89-82f3"], "assigner": "Linux", "epss": 0.21, "enisaIdProduct": [{"id": "0bf2f26f-6125-3ce9-9ce1-f5c51c347db5", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "ce514124161ac2ceb13d10b6c40cbf05c8f0cc91 <bffd0655a35402b2df8857699f8248e5a534d214"}, {"id": "1055f95b-89a2-30d6-86c4-8b65f0a2f71d", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 5.15.221"}, {"id": "1781cfe4-9136-38d7-bd38-8d01846155fa", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "ce514124161ac2ceb13d10b6c40cbf05c8f0cc91 <1135d6875d2dbda3f6ec718f3421a6ce4378bd63"}, {"id": "254b18ae-f0b5-34e8-bf11-9e9a924fbdbb", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_ver